WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:04.278
Polonius was reading in his study when Ophelia entered.

2
00:00:04.279 --> 00:00:08.651
"Oh Father," she cried. "I’m worried about Hamlet!

3
00:00:08.652 --> 00:00:14.810
He came to see me just now, his clothing in disarray, with a pitiful look on his face.

4
00:00:14.811 --> 00:00:18.373
He wouldn’t speak; he just stared at me.

5
00:00:18.374 --> 00:00:27.356
He kept nodding his head, and he sighed so loudly his whole body shook. And then, still staring at me, he left!"

6
00:00:27.357 --> 00:00:32.214
"Oh dear," said Polonius. "Have you spoken to him harshly of late?"

7
00:00:32.215 --> 00:00:37.328
"No, but I did as you ordered." Ophelia hung her head in sorrow.

8
00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:40.241
"I told him I couldn’t see him anymore."

9
00:00:40.242 --> 00:00:48.661
"Your rejection has made him mad, I fear. I must tell the king; he too has wondered about Hamlet’s odd behavior lately."

10
00:00:48.662 --> 00:00:56.685
Hamlet’s mother and his uncle Claudius were in the great hall with Hamlet’s childhood friends Rosencrantz and Guildenstern.

11
00:00:56.686 --> 00:01:04.265
"I summoned you two to court," said the king, "because I believe something other than his father’s death is troubling Hamlet.

12
00:01:04.266 --> 00:01:09.019
Spend time with him and report anything you find out to me."

13
00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:15.035
"You will be rewarded generously," Gertrude added. She was very worried about her son.

14
00:01:15.036 --> 00:01:19.622
"We shall obey your majesties," said Rosencrantz, bowing low.

15
00:01:19.623 --> 00:01:25.400
"At your service, your majesties," said Guildenstern, bowing even lower.

16
00:01:25.401 --> 00:01:28.263
Just then Polonius entered the hall.

17
00:01:28.264 --> 00:01:32.852
"Good news, my lord! The ambassadors have returned from Norway.

18
00:01:32.853 --> 00:01:38.280
Fortinbras has agreed not to invade our country. Denmark is safe."

19
00:01:38.281 --> 00:01:40.716
"Excellent," said Claudius.

20
00:01:40.717 --> 00:01:46.851
"I have more news," Polonius continued. "I know what is making Hamlet crazy.

21
00:01:46.852 --> 00:01:52.573
He has been courting my daughter, Ophelia, and I told her she should discourage him.

22
00:01:52.574 --> 00:01:57.209
After all he is a prince, but she is not a princess.

23
00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:02.524
When she told him she could not see him anymore, it broke his heart and drove him mad." "I’m

24
00:02:02.525 --> 00:02:08.644
not so sure that’s the reason," said the king, frowning. "Can you give me any proof?" "Certainly,

25
00:02:08.645 --> 00:02:15.549
my lord. I’ll arrange for us to secretly observe them together, so you can judge for yourself. We

26
00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:24.534
can hide behind the tapestries here in the great hall, where they often meet. I’ll tell Ophelia to wait for Hamlet here this afternoon." "Arrange

27
00:02:24.535 --> 00:02:27.025
it," said Claudius. In

28
00:02:27.026 --> 00:02:31.977
another hall in the castle, Rosencrantz and Guildenstern found Hamlet. "Why

29
00:02:31.978 --> 00:02:35.041
are you here?" asked the prince. "To

30
00:02:35.042 --> 00:02:38.827
visit you!" replied Rosencrantz cheerily. "Didn’t

31
00:02:38.828 --> 00:02:43.406
the king send for you?" asked Hamlet suspiciously. Guildenstern

32
00:02:43.407 --> 00:02:47.031
glanced nervously at Rosencrantz. "The

33
00:02:47.032 --> 00:02:51.760
king said you needed cheering up," Rosencrantz said smoothly. "And

34
00:02:51.761 --> 00:02:56.633
we have just the thing to lift your spirits," said Guildenstern. "On

35
00:02:56.634 --> 00:03:02.609
our journey we met a traveling theater company. They’ll perform a play here tonight." Trumpets

36
00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:06.260
sounded, and the actors entered the hall. "I

37
00:03:06.261 --> 00:03:11.308
know these actors," Hamlet exclaimed, his face lighting up. "Welcome!" Then

38
00:03:11.309 --> 00:03:19.759
he had an idea. He drew one of the actors aside and asked, "Can you perform The Murder of Gonzago ?"

39
00:03:19.759 --> 00:03:22.718
"Certainly, my lord," replied the actor.

40
00:03:22.719 --> 00:03:28.345
"Good," said Hamlet. "And I’d like you to add a few lines that I will write."

41
00:03:28.346 --> 00:03:34.842
He turned to Rosencrantz and Guildenstern. "Now, friends, show the actors to their rooms."

42
00:03:34.843 --> 00:03:38.547
When everyone had left, Hamlet considered his plan.

43
00:03:38.548 --> 00:03:46.163
"The play I chose should provide proof that my uncle killed my father. It is about the murder of a king.

44
00:03:46.164 --> 00:03:53.332
If Claudius is guilty, he will react when he sees it. If he flinches even once, I’ll know!

45
00:03:53.333 --> 00:04:01.388
Yes, the play’s the thing wherein I’ll catch the conscience of the king!" He started to walk to his chambers.

46
00:04:01.389 --> 00:04:05.175
But as he walked, Hamlet began to doubt himself.

47
00:04:05.176 --> 00:04:11.659
"Why has it taken me so long to avenge my father’s death? Am I a coward?" he thought.

48
00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:17.015
He became so distressed about his situation that he began to contemplate suicide.

49
00:04:17.016 --> 00:04:21.596
"To be or not to be: that is the question.

50
00:04:21.597 --> 00:04:29.285
Is it nobler to deal with the blows that fate sends you, or to simply put a stop to them by ending your own life?

51
00:04:29.286 --> 00:04:37.903
Oh, to die, to sleep . . . but that’s what we’re afraid of—that sleep of death from which no traveler returns.

52
00:04:37.904 --> 00:04:40.901
That’s what makes us fight for life."

53
00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:47.535
As Hamlet passed through the great hall, he ran into Ophelia. She looked up from a book as he entered.

54
00:04:47.536 --> 00:04:52.590
"My lord," said Ophelia, "I want to return the gifts you gave me."

55
00:04:52.591 --> 00:04:55.170
"I gave you nothing," said Hamlet.

56
00:04:55.171 --> 00:04:58.852
"You know you did," replied Ophelia, confused.

57
00:04:58.853 --> 00:05:02.725
"I loved you once, but no longer," said Hamlet.

58
00:05:02.726 --> 00:05:06.511
"Then I was deceived," said Ophelia, deeply hurt.

59
00:05:06.512 --> 00:05:09.931
"You should go to a convent," Hamlet told her.

60
00:05:09.932 --> 00:05:14.408
"I’m not worth your time. We men are proud and vengeful.

61
00:05:14.409 --> 00:05:22.662
And you women make fools of us! We’ll have no more marriage! Get thee to a nunnery!" He turned and left the room.

62
00:05:22.663 --> 00:05:30.678
"Heaven help him!" cried Ophelia. "Such a noble mind gone mad! Oh, woe is me!"

63
00:05:30.679 --> 00:05:37.337
Claudius and Polonius came out from behind a tapestry. They had been eavesdropping on the conversation.

64
00:05:37.338 --> 00:05:40.806
"I don’t believe he’s lovesick," declared the king.

65
00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:48.512
"I think something else is troubling him, and when it surfaces, it could be dangerous. I’ll send him to England."

66
00:05:48.513 --> 00:05:53.949
"I still think the problem is love," said Polonius, stroking his beard thoughtfully.

67
00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:58.758
"Ask the queen to speak to him tonight. Hamlet will be honest with her.

68
00:05:58.759 --> 00:06:02.781
I will hide myself so I can hear their conversation. If

69
00:06:02.782 --> 00:06:07.718
a broken heart is not his problem, then send him to England immediately." "It

70
00:06:07.719 --> 00:06:14.733
shall be so," replied the king. "Madness in great ones must not unwatched go." That

71
00:06:14.734 --> 00:06:19.859
evening, before the play, Hamlet explained his plan to Horatio. "Watch

72
00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:24.105
the king’s reaction carefully," he told his friend. A

73
00:06:24.106 --> 00:06:28.153
stage lit by torches had been set up in the great hall. Claudius,

74
00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:33.731
Gertrude, Polonius, and the courtiers seated themselves in front of it. Two

75
00:06:33.732 --> 00:06:37.953
actors entered, dressed as a king and a queen. "The

76
00:06:37.954 --> 00:06:43.660
play is called The Murder of Gonzago ," said Hamlet to the people around him.

77
00:06:43.661 --> 00:06:47.529
"Gonzago is the king. It’s based on a true story."

78
00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:56.745
"We have been married thirty years," said the player king, "and our love is still strong. But I grow old and soon will die!"

79
00:06:56.746 --> 00:07:02.302
"I love you so much that I will never marry again!" declared the player queen.

80
00:07:02.303 --> 00:07:11.240
Gonzago then said he was sleepy and would rest in the garden, and the player queen left the stage. A third actor appeared.

81
00:07:11.241 --> 00:07:20.271
"I am Lucianus, the king’s nephew," said the actor, "but I long to be king!" He held up a small glass vial.

82
00:07:20.272 --> 00:07:23.866
"This poison can kill a man instantly!"

83
00:07:23.867 --> 00:07:31.294
He crept over to the player king, who lay asleep, and tipped the bottle of poison into the player king’s ear.

84
00:07:31.295 --> 00:07:38.858
At this Claudius rose so swiftly that he knocked over his chair. "Lights, lights!" he thundered.

85
00:07:38.859 --> 00:07:42.374
"Are you ill, my lord?" said Gertrude, alarmed.

86
00:07:42.375 --> 00:07:51.624
"Away!" cried Claudius. He swept out of the hall, followed by Gertrude and the entire court, except for Hamlet and Horatio.

87
00:07:51.625 --> 00:07:55.566
"Did you see that?" said Hamlet excitedly to his friend.

88
00:07:55.574 --> 00:08:00.097
"Oh Horatio, I believe the ghost now!"

